"transactions itself, so nothing is added)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The method is a GraphQL operation (`@Query`, `@Mutation`, `@Subscription`,\n"
"`@Name`, `@Resolver` or a `@Source` method) on a `@GraphQLApi` class."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The method returns a blocking type. Reactive return types (`Uni`, `Multi`,\n"
"`CompletionStage`, `CompletableFuture` or `Publisher`) are never made\n"
"transactional."
msgstr ""

msgid "The method is not annotated with `@NonBlocking`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The method is not already annotated with `@Transactional` (an explicit\n"
"annotation always wins)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To opt a specific operation out of this behavior - for example when the\n"
"resolver calls a library that manages its own JDBC transactions - annotate "
"it\n"
"with `@Transactional(Transactional.TxType.NOT_SUPPORTED)`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also use any other `TxType` (such as `REQUIRES_NEW`) to control how "
"the\n"
"operation participates in transactions, since an explicit `@Transactional`\n"
"takes precedence over the implicit one."
msgstr ""

